  "chromeText": "Robot Wiki Citation-first encyclopedia of modern robot learning. Robot Wiki is an encyclopedia of modern robotics for engineers who already know machine learning: learned manipulation policies, sim-to-real reinforcement learning, world models, teleoperation data pipelines, and the classical control stack underneath. Technical claims should be traceable to cited evidence. Sources range from research papers to first-party documentation and labelled community estimates, and a citation is not a guarantee of verification. The centre of gravity is robot learning, not a catalogue of the industry. Start reading How to read this wiki | Robot Wiki | Domain index | Featured interactive |  |  | Reset | 25%50%75%100%050100steps | Real hardware | A Boston Dynamics Spot quadruped walks with Royal Air Force airmen at RAF Leeming during the Agile Liberty 21-2 technology trials in August 2021. | Interactive tools | 100 mm | 3D Kinematics Playground | Market Map | Learning paths | Robot learning and VLA | Classical robotics foundations | World models for robotics | How to read this wiki | A yellow Boston Dynamics Spot quadruped robot walks across an airfield tarmac alongside Royal Air Force airmen in camouflage uniform. | Introduction | Per-step success probability in percent, currently 95.0 | Episode length in steps, currently 30 | Line chart of episode success against episode length at 95.0 percent per-step success | Side view of the shipped SO-101 arm at its zero configuration, 6 revolute joints from the base to the gripper",
